\subsection{\code{OAuthConnection$access_token()}}{
  Get a current bearer token for an SDK or database driver, refreshing when
needed. Obtain this connection from a module's \code{connection()} method.
The method refreshes credentials when needed, without starting login,
requesting new permissions or retrying the SDK operation.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{OAuthConnection$access_token(
  required_scopes = character(),
  min_valid_for = 60,
  force_refresh = FALSE,
  async = FALSE,
  target = NULL
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{required_scopes}}{Permissions needed for this operation, in addition to
client requirements. This checks permissions without changing the grant.}
      \item{\code{min_valid_for}}{Minimum remaining lifetime in seconds (default 60).
Allow time for the operation and clock differences. Unknown or insufficient
expiry triggers refresh; an unusable replacement raises an error.}
      \item{\code{force_refresh}}{Require a new token even if a cached one is usable.
Refresh coordination and provider retry delays still apply.}
      \item{\code{async}}{If \code{TRUE}, return a promise, including for a cached token.
If \code{FALSE}, return a string or raise an error; a synchronous call cannot
wait for an already running async refresh.}
      \item{\code{target}}{Optional API name from \code{token_targets}. \code{NULL} selects the
client's default. Its token is acquired when needed.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors can indicate an unavailable login, insufficient permission, pending or
failed refresh, or an unsuitable token lifetime. Stable reason names include
\code{authorization_unavailable}, \code{insufficient_scope}, \code{refresh_pending},
\code{refresh_unavailable}, \code{interaction_required}, \code{lifetime_unavailable},
\code{unsupported_token_binding}, \code{unknown_target} and \code{unsupported_target}.
See \code{vignette("external-integrations", package = "shinyOAuth")}
(\href{https://lukakoning.github.io/shinyOAuth/articles/external-integrations.html}{online guide})
for error recovery and async examples.

DPoP and mTLS-bound tokens require their signing key or certificate; use
\verb{$request()} instead of exporting a bearer string. Exported tokens retain all
provider-issued permissions, which may exceed the app's local operation limits.
Recheck the current login and permissions before using an async token snapshot.
Acquiring a token does not extend a managed owner's inactivity limit.
